has views on everything, from the latest tactical fad to Chris Sutton=E2=80=
=99s choice of dinner. This overload has led to some Peterborough fans ques=
tioning whether he is committed enough to the day job of managing their rel=
egation-threatened League One club. =E2=80=9CIt=E2=80=99s all about winning=
 games of football,=E2=80=9D honked Savage, who has won only two matches in=
 eight since taking over (one against Ipswich Under-21s). =E2=80=9CThe narr=
ative can be spun in any way but I=E2=80=99m a football man. It=E2=80=99s m=
y life. It=E2=80=99s what I love doing and I love watching football. I=E2=
=80=99m not somebody who goes home and sits in front of the TV, or goes to =
the pub or has any hobbies outside of football. I=E2=80=99m not a golfer. I=
 just love football. I=E2=80=99ll go and watch every game that I can. I=E2=
=80=99m very fortunate that when I go and do games for TNT or 606, I=E2=80=
=99m getting knowledge all the time =E2=80=A6 It hurts the fans the most wh=
en we lose, it hurts me a lot. But it=E2=80=99s a narrative that gets creat=
ed if we=E2=80=99re not winning games.=E2=80=9D To which many Posh fans wou=
ld say: so win some then!</p></div></td></tr>
